FSM Framework (pgfsm) is licensed per component. See SPEC-017,
docs/specs/spec-017-licensing-agpl-core-apache-sdks.md.

The engine, which users reach only over a protocol (Postgres, HTTP, TCP), is
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only
(LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt):

  packages/database-src/            fsm_core (SQL, migrations, install SQL,
                                    PGXN bundle), except its contract files
                                    listed below
  packages/database-src-extension/  fsm_core as a pgrx extension
  packages/fsm-api-ts/              @pgfsm/api
  packages/fsm-async-worker-gateway-ts/
                                    @pgfsm/async-worker-gateway (the Activity
                                    Gateway)

Everything else is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt), including everything users' code runs in, links or
copies: the async-worker SDKs, the proto contracts and generated stubs,
@pgfsm/sync-worker, @pgfsm/db, @pgfsm/logging, @pgfsm/compiler, @pgfsm/cli and
the projects it generates, @pgfsm/ctl, examples, test apps and docs. That also
covers fsm_core's public contract inside packages/database-src/:

  packages/database-src/fsm.machine.schema.*.json
  packages/database-src/xstate.machine.schema.json
  packages/database-src/generated/

REUSE.toml is the authoritative, machine-readable form of this mapping, and
each package directory carries the LICENSE file for its licence.

Versions released before this licensing took effect, including fsm_core 1.2.0,
remain available under the licence they were released under.
